72 #uuid "85c3a288-e595-578f-a534-db75ed9d872f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393208 #edb/ref 1074 "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2}+xy+2x)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2}+xy+2x)\\,j \\\\  & =(2{y}^{2}+y+2)\\,i+(4xy+x)\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1) & =(2(1)^{2}+(1)+2)\\,i+(4(1)(1)+(1))\\,j \\\\  & =5\\,i+5\\,j \\\\  & =⟨5,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨5,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393209 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393209 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393209 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393212 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393209 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393209 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393214 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393209 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393209 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393209 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186393214 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393209 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d2b7a822-706f-59e1-aaeb-ea5e1255d429" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393210 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393210 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393210 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f817dec0-31ee-5a90-a6ae-2391b9cf9403" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393211 #ed